	"bugClass": {
		"id": "singleton-segmented-style-conflict",
		"title": "Singleton segmented controls inherit unintended active styling",
		"cause": "A shared CSS selector targets an active button when it is the only child, causing singleton segmented groups to receive styling intended for a different state or context. The selector does not account for independent groups or the state-specific visual treatment required by the viewport.",
		"criteria": "Match when a stylesheet has a singleton structural selector such as :only-child or :only-of-type combined with active/selected state and segmented-control button styling, and that rule can override state-specific styling across independently rendered groups. Each conflicting singleton selector is sufficient; neutral singleton styling without a state conflict does not match.",
